      "id": 14,
      "options": {
        "content": "### Prometheus Metrics vs `/gateway/dashboard` Parity\n\n| Prometheus Metric | Metric Type | Labels | `/gateway/dashboard` JSON Field |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `gateway_requests_total` | Counter | `method`, `route`, `status_code` | `services[<svc>].requests`, `routes[<route>].requests` |\n| `gateway_request_duration_seconds` | Histogram | `method`, `route` | `services[<svc>].latency_p50`, `services[<svc>].latency_p95`, `routes[<route>].latency_histogram` |\n| `gateway_errors_total` | Counter | `method`, `route` | `services[<svc>].errors`, `routes[<route>].errors`, `routes[<route>].error_rate` |\n| `gateway_circuit_breaker_state` | Gauge | `service` | `services[<svc>].circuit_breaker_state`, `circuit_breakers[<svc>].state` (0=closed, 1=half-open, 2=open) |\n| `gateway_cache_hit_rate` | Gauge | `service` | `services[<svc>].cache_hit_rate`, `cache.by_service[<svc>].hit_rate` (0.0\u2013100.0) |\n\n> **Synchronization Architecture**:\n> The `/metrics` endpoint executes `sync_gauges_from_collector()` before generating Prometheus output, synchronizing the in-memory `MetricsCollector` state with Prometheus Gauges so both endpoints reflect identical telemetry.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
